---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Ebb - Support"
  description="Get help with Ebb - Breathing Exercises, the iOS app: picking a pattern, breathing with your eyes closed, the widgets and daily nudge, Apple Watch, importing from Breathe Easy, and Apple Health."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/ebb/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Ebb?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Ebb%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Which pattern should I pick?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">On Today, pick what you need and Ebb suggests one: coherent breathing to calm down, 4-7-8 to wind down, box breathing to focus, Nadi Shodhana for balance, pursed-lip to slow down, and Ujjayi for its soft ocean sound. Every pattern is also in the Patterns tab.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I breathe with my eyes closed?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Ebb taps at every change of breath: rising taps to breathe in, two light ticks to hold, falling taps to breathe out. Turn on Ocean sound in Settings to hear the tide too. Haptic cues can be turned off under Breathing.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I start without opening the app?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Add the Take a breath widget to your Home Screen (touch and hold the Home Screen, tap Edit, then Add Widget, and choose Ebb) and tap a length. You can also add Breathe to Control Center or the Action button, or say &ldquo;Breathe with Ebb&rdquo; to Siri.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I set up the daily nudge?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Tap the settings button on Today, then under Daily nudge choose a time and the days you&rsquo;d like. Long-press the nudge to start straight from it. It&rsquo;s skipped on days you&rsquo;ve already breathed.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does the Apple Watch keep going with my wrist down?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. A session on the watch keeps its timing and taps with the screen off, and joins your iPhone&rsquo;s Log when it&rsquo;s done.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I move my history over from Breathe Easy?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">In Ebb, open Settings and tap Import from Breathe Easy under Your data. Ebb uses the same six patterns, so every session comes over as it was, minutes and all.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How does Apple Health work?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">In Settings, turn on Save mindful minutes. Each session you finish is saved to Apple Health as mindful minutes, not counting pauses. Ebb never reads anything from Health.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Is Ebb free?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Everything in Ebb is free, with no ads or subscription. If you&rsquo;d like to support it, Settings &rarr; Support Ebb has optional one-time tips. They don&rsquo;t unlock anything, and they&rsquo;re handled entirely by the App Store.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can Ebb move less?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Ebb follows Reduce Motion: turn it on in the iPhone Settings app under Accessibility &rarr; Motion. Ebb holds still and the water changes tone with each breath instead of rising.</p>
            </div>

            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">I feel dizzy. What should I do?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Stop and breathe normally. Ebb is for relaxation, not medical care. If you have a heart or lung condition, or are pregnant, check with your doctor before trying breath holds.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
